.TH STEN 1 "September 2026" "sten 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sten \- ScatterBit steganography for images (pure C, no libraries)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sten encode
.RI \-i " image" " \-o " output
.RB "(\-m " text " | \-f " file )
.RB "[ \-k " key " | \-p " passphrase ]
.br
.B sten decode
.RI \-i " image"
.RB "[ \-k " key " | \-p " passphrase ]
.br
.B sten capacity
.RI \-i " image
.br
.B sten inspect
.RI \-i " image
.PP
.B sten
.RB "\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help"\fR |
.B "\-V\fR | \fB\-\-version"\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sten
hides a message inside an image by modifying its least significant bytes
using a pseudo-random ScatterBit walk, so the payload is spread over the
whole carrier. The modified image keeps its format and stays visually
unchanged. It is written in pure C with no external libraries.
.PP
Supported carrier formats:
.BR BMP ", " PNG ", " GIF ", " JPEG ", " PNM/PAM ", " TGA ", " TIFF ", " ICO .
For formats that save size explicitly (PNG, JPEG, PNM/PAM, TGA, TIFF, ICO)
the pixel data is never re-encoded; the original bytes are reused, splicing
new chunks in when needed. JPEG files are never recompressed: messages ride
in a new or existing COM (comment) segment.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B encode
Hides
.I text
(option
.B \-m
or
.B \-f
for a file; stdin when both are absent and stdin is not a terminal) inside
.RI image
and writes the result to
.I output
(options
.BR \-i ", " \-o ).
.TP
.B decode
Extracts the message from
.RI image
and prints it to stdout. Exit status 1 means the image is clean or the
wrong key was used.
.TP
.B capacity
Prints the number of message bytes
.RI image
can hold.
.TP
.B inspect
Prints the format, dimensions, color layout and capacity of
.IR image .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-i, \-\-input " image
Input image.
.TP
.BI "\-o, \-\-output " image
Output image
.RB ( encode
only).
.TP
.BI "\-m, \-\-message " text
Text message to hide.
.TP
.BI "\-f, \-\-file " file
Read the message from a file.
.TP
.BI "\-k, \-\-key " key
Optional key. It only derives the ScatterBit path (a seed); it does not
encrypt the payload.
.TP
.BI "\-p, \-\-passphrase " passphrase
Optional passphrase. Derives a bit path and encrypts the payload with
ChaCha20, itself keyed by PBKDF2\-HMAC\-SHA256. With
.B \-p
the length of the hidden message is also obfuscated (a fixed-size random
padding, stored length, decrypted payload and a checksum are hidden).
.TP
.BR "\-v, \-\-verbose"
Print details about the detected format to standard error.
.TP
.BR "\-h, \-\-help"
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR "\-V, \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Exactly one of
.B \-m
and
.B \-f
may be used; exactly one of
.B \-k
and
.B \-p
may be used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No message found (clean image or wrong key).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Operational error (unreadable/unsupported/corrupt image, message too large,
I/O failure).
.SH SECURITY
.I sten
is not encryption. Anyone who knows the image can try to extract the
payload; use
.B \-p
when the message must be protected, and strong keys when deriving paths is
sensitive. The COM-only JPEG backend keeps pixels untouched, so capacity is
unrelated to image size.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I docs/sten.1
This manual page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR make (1).
.PP
Source repository and the ROADMAP with the expected \\fBCompresión real\\fR
efforts: hide the message, then deflate it before hiding; or compress the
ZIGZAG stream. Run \\fBmake test\\fR, \\fBmake fuzz-san\\fR and
\\fBmake test-san\\fR for verification.